705
00:40:35,717 --> 00:40:36,957
[SPEAKER_01]: They didn't know.

706
00:40:37,298 --> 00:40:38,198
[SPEAKER_01]: Couldn't do nothing about it.

707
00:40:39,859 --> 00:40:40,680
[SPEAKER_01]: He was a big group.

708
00:40:42,441 --> 00:40:42,601
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

709
00:40:42,621 --> 00:40:45,003
[SPEAKER_01]: As long as he could produce, I guess they couldn't say much.

710
00:40:45,023 --> 00:40:50,807
[SPEAKER_02]: You know, one time, Lazari and I, we never went down for breakfast.

711
00:40:50,907 --> 00:40:52,529
[SPEAKER_02]: Always had our breakfast thrown up in the room.

712
00:40:54,310 --> 00:40:54,990
[SPEAKER_02]: Some rookie.

713
00:40:57,132 --> 00:41:00,414
[SPEAKER_02]: He always had breakfast in the room and, uh, managed it.

714
00:41:00,434 --> 00:41:00,955
[SPEAKER_01]: Charles, pardon me.

715
00:41:00,975 --> 00:41:02,936
[SPEAKER_01]: Pick up the phone and say hello to your sister.

716
00:41:02,956 --> 00:41:07,680
[SPEAKER_00]: She tried to put everything out of my reach and all, make me work.

717
00:41:08,621 --> 00:41:09,041
[SPEAKER_00]: You know,

718
00:41:10,137 --> 00:41:14,060
[SPEAKER_00]: I know because my mother, I'm telling you why, my mother was in Highland View.

719
00:41:15,040 --> 00:41:19,283
[SPEAKER_00]: And she was so frustrated anyway, because she was real active, I suppose the way you were.

720
00:41:19,764 --> 00:41:29,110
[SPEAKER_00]: And when Nan, oh she would get so mad, and my dad would have everything just a little bit farther, and when she would make it that farther, she'd move a little bit farther away.

721
00:41:29,430 --> 00:41:31,932
[SPEAKER_00]: I said, that must have been their whole philosophy in Highland View.

722
00:41:33,373 --> 00:41:34,013
[SPEAKER_02]: She had a stroke?

723
00:41:34,293 --> 00:41:38,396
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, she had a, in fact, she had about 12 of them within three years.

724
00:41:39,029 --> 00:41:42,371
[SPEAKER_00]: This is my second in three years.

725
00:41:44,132 --> 00:41:51,217
[SPEAKER_02]: I had a stroke and I had two heart attacks after that.

726
00:41:51,237 --> 00:41:54,619
[SPEAKER_02]: Then after I got over the heart attacks, I had a kidney infection.

727
00:41:55,279 --> 00:41:57,680
[SPEAKER_02]: I had to get an operation off the kidneys.

728
00:42:00,022 --> 00:42:01,503
[SPEAKER_02]: Of course, they do that now today.

729
00:42:01,523 --> 00:42:02,644
[SPEAKER_02]: They don't touch you up anymore.

730
00:42:04,244 --> 00:42:05,005
[SPEAKER_02]: They use tubes.

731
00:42:08,820 --> 00:42:13,101
[SPEAKER_01]: What was his story about you and Lazari had breakfast and Ms. Brook eat?

732
00:42:13,302 --> 00:42:16,082
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, we used to have our breakfast every morning in the room.

733
00:42:17,343 --> 00:42:18,703
[SPEAKER_02]: Not our dinners, but our breakfast.

734
00:42:19,784 --> 00:42:21,784
[SPEAKER_02]: Too lazy to go downstairs, and I didn't want to get dressed.

735
00:42:24,045 --> 00:42:31,608
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you know, when Walter left town, the hotel would send all the bills to New York.

736
00:42:31,628 --> 00:42:35,449
[SPEAKER_02]: You could see who was eating downstairs, who was eating in the room.

737
00:42:36,790 --> 00:42:38,210
[SPEAKER_02]: So this kid, you know, Ms. Brook,

738
00:42:38,993 --> 00:42:41,894
[SPEAKER_02]: He had breakfast in the room, and Carthy challenged him on it.

739
00:42:41,914 --> 00:42:47,957
[SPEAKER_02]: He says, how come you think we usually have breakfast in the room?

740
00:42:47,997 --> 00:42:50,418
[SPEAKER_02]: He says, well, what's so bad about that?

741
00:42:50,438 --> 00:42:51,819
[SPEAKER_02]: He says, well, what's so bad about it?

742
00:42:52,339 --> 00:42:53,019
[SPEAKER_02]: You're just a rookie.

743
00:42:53,039 --> 00:42:55,960
[SPEAKER_02]: Get down and have your breakfast and let the rest of them do it.

744
00:42:55,980 --> 00:42:59,502
[SPEAKER_02]: He says, Rafael Nazari doesn't have breakfast on every morning.

745
00:43:00,462 --> 00:43:02,243
[SPEAKER_02]: He said, let me tell you something.

746
00:43:02,263 --> 00:43:03,944
[SPEAKER_02]: These are two established ballplayers.

747
00:43:04,344 --> 00:43:05,424
[SPEAKER_02]: You're not established yet.

748
00:43:05,444 --> 00:43:06,585
[SPEAKER_02]: You didn't make the club yet.

749
00:43:09,067 --> 00:43:10,248
[SPEAKER_02]: So this kid was telling us about it.

750
00:43:10,868 --> 00:43:12,730
[SPEAKER_02]: I said, well, let me give you some good advice, son.

751
00:43:16,873 --> 00:43:19,956
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, was there a, he was an epileptic?

752
00:43:21,056 --> 00:43:22,698
[SPEAKER_01]: Did he have any attacks that he had?

753
00:43:22,918 --> 00:43:24,559
[SPEAKER_02]: He had one when I was there, yeah.

754
00:43:24,659 --> 00:43:32,826
[SPEAKER_02]: I had a fellow one morning there and he was out of bed just laying on the floor, you know, jumping around and shaking.

755
00:43:32,846 --> 00:43:33,606
[SPEAKER_02]: He got scared as hell.

756
00:43:33,626 --> 00:43:34,447
[SPEAKER_02]: I don't know what the hell to do.

757
00:43:34,467 --> 00:43:38,310
[SPEAKER_02]: I run out of room in my pajamas for help.

758
00:43:39,692 --> 00:43:40,753
[SPEAKER_01]: He didn't know he had this.

759
00:43:41,914 --> 00:43:44,636
[SPEAKER_01]: He didn't tell him about it, how it affected him.

760
00:43:49,520 --> 00:43:51,641
[SPEAKER_01]: He never had an attack on the field, I guess, did he?

761
00:43:51,681 --> 00:43:51,861
[SPEAKER_02]: No.

