00:45:45,708 --> 00:45:46,848
[SPEAKER_01]: He got us in trouble, didn't he?

792
00:45:51,309 --> 00:45:52,829
[SPEAKER_02]: My crusaders used to drive me crazy.

793
00:45:55,950 --> 00:45:57,750
[SPEAKER_02]: They'd give me some runs, you know, and very seldom.

794
00:45:57,770 --> 00:45:59,371
[SPEAKER_02]: They didn't ever like to make any runs for me.

795
00:45:59,991 --> 00:46:06,532
[SPEAKER_02]: They'd rather send me a pitch to one or nothing game or two to one than they would give me another run because I started experimenting, see.

796
00:46:06,552 --> 00:46:09,513
[SPEAKER_02]: And just so they made a lot of runs, the crusaders would get mad, go all the way out there,

797
00:46:10,572 --> 00:46:17,013
[SPEAKER_02]: and go up to the show stop and yell, OK, Ruffin, go ahead, Edison, go ahead, Thomas Edison, show us what you got, man.

798
00:46:18,553 --> 00:46:22,874
[SPEAKER_02]: And I'd start laughing, you know, and I'd start fooling around with slow curves and all that.

799
00:46:22,914 --> 00:46:24,834
[SPEAKER_02]: He'd say, there you go, that's a boy.

800
00:46:26,875 --> 00:46:28,635
[SPEAKER_02]: I'd be no good SB.

801
00:46:28,655 --> 00:46:30,175
[SPEAKER_02]: He'd say, I don't want to get married this fall.

802
00:46:30,715 --> 00:46:31,676
[SPEAKER_02]: I need the extra money.

803
00:46:33,456 --> 00:46:36,256
[SPEAKER_02]: Then when he got married, he had a kid, and then I had all I heard about the kid.

804
00:46:38,017 --> 00:46:40,357
[SPEAKER_02]: When he had a 2-1 game, he knew he didn't have to worry about it.

805
00:46:41,689 --> 00:46:43,129
[SPEAKER_02]: He said, you know what, bear down.

806
00:46:43,930 --> 00:46:49,992
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, I just started making a lot of runs, and he started mowing out there.

807
00:46:50,012 --> 00:46:51,652
[SPEAKER_01]: You really experimented, I would assume.

808
00:46:52,353 --> 00:46:53,393
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I got a lot of runs, yeah.

809
00:46:53,453 --> 00:46:56,894
[SPEAKER_01]: What did McCarty think about that?

810
00:46:57,654 --> 00:46:58,234
[SPEAKER_01]: He didn't like it.

811
00:46:59,995 --> 00:47:00,975
[SPEAKER_02]: He couldn't do nothing about it.

812
00:47:05,337 --> 00:47:05,977
[SPEAKER_02]: You know, he...

813
00:47:10,842 --> 00:47:19,085
[SPEAKER_02]: I went back to Yankee's old timer's day one time, and Mrs. MacArthur was there, and she called me over.

814
00:47:20,325 --> 00:47:21,465
[SPEAKER_02]: She said, Red, can I see you a minute?

815
00:47:22,026 --> 00:47:22,646
[SPEAKER_01]: I said, sure.

816
00:47:23,886 --> 00:47:25,427
[SPEAKER_02]: She said, I got something I want to tell you.

817
00:47:25,447 --> 00:47:27,027
[SPEAKER_02]: She said, I couldn't tell you when you was pitching.

818
00:47:27,988 --> 00:47:32,569
[SPEAKER_02]: And she said, I just wanted to see you.

819
00:47:32,589 --> 00:47:35,230
[SPEAKER_02]: And Mrs. MacArthur was there, and she called me over.

820
00:47:36,450 --> 00:47:37,611
[SPEAKER_02]: She said, Red, can I see you a minute?

821
00:47:38,151 --> 00:47:38,751
[SPEAKER_01]: I said, sure.

822
00:47:40,302 --> 00:47:41,563
[SPEAKER_02]: I said, I got something I want to tell you.

823
00:47:41,583 --> 00:47:43,164
[SPEAKER_02]: She said, I couldn't tell you when you was pitching.

824
00:47:44,045 --> 00:47:45,286
[SPEAKER_02]: She said, I can tell you now.

825
00:47:46,867 --> 00:47:48,368
[SPEAKER_02]: She says, you know one thing?

826
00:47:49,328 --> 00:47:54,412
[SPEAKER_02]: Joe McCarty, my husband, never slept good until you was pitching the next day.

827
00:47:55,653 --> 00:47:58,235
[SPEAKER_02]: But when you was pitching that day, he said, that's the only time he relaxed.

828
00:48:00,236 --> 00:48:01,277
[SPEAKER_02]: That's just nice to hear.

829
00:48:02,998 --> 00:48:03,558
[SPEAKER_02]: She told me that.

830
00:48:03,578 --> 00:48:05,680
[SPEAKER_02]: She said, the only time he relaxed.

